  "worked_solution": "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},\u2026,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2.5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, & \\,{m}_{4} & =1.5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5, & \\,{x}_{4} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =2.5\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 5+1.5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =5+6+5+9 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$",
